    "name": "Reports - Force Evaluate",
    "description": "# Reports — Force Evaluate\n\nForce a medrecord booking to evaluation **done** (`for_evaluation = 2`) and mark it as force-evaluated so the daily medrecord cron does not overwrite those flags.\n\n## Auth\n- Header: `API-KEY` (required)\n- Body: `token`, `requester` (required)\n\n## Endpoint\n`POST /reports/force_evaluate`\n\n## Payload\n| Field | Required | Notes |\n|-------|----------|-------|\n| `token` | yes | Auth token |\n| `requester` | yes | User id — also stored as `force_evaluate_by` |\n| `medrecord_id` | yes | Report DB `medrecord.id` (any row of the booking) |\n\n## Effects\n1. Loads the medrecord by `medrecord_id`\n2. Updates **all** non-deleted rows for the same `branch_id` + `booking_id`:\n   - `for_evaluation` → `2` (done)\n   - `is_force_evaluate` → `1`\n   - `force_evaluate_by` → `requester`\n   - `force_evaluate_on` → now\n3. If `endorsement_id` is present and non-zero:\n   - `for_release` → `2`\n   - `for_release_log` → email/print log ids for that booking\n\n## Cron protection\nETL delete skips `is_force_evaluate = 1`. Upsert keeps forced `for_evaluation` / `for_release` / `for_release_log` / audit columns.\n\nDoes **not** clear pending specimen/result/recollection buckets or create EMR evaluation records.\n\n## Label legend\n`0` = no, `1` = yes, `2` = done, `3` = n_a\n",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
